From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [sensord] Handle local socket errors with Qt 5.15 and Qt 6

SocketHandler connected each client socket's error signal by name, as
error(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError). Qt 5.15 renamed that signal to
errorOccurred() and Qt 6 removed the old name, so built against Qt 6 the
connect only printed

  QObject::connect: No such signal QLocalSocket::error(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError)

on every new client and socket errors never reached socketError().

Connect to errorOccurred() by pointer from Qt 5.15 on, so a missing signal
is a build error rather than a runtime warning, and keep the connect by
name for older Qt, where it still works and nothing changes.

Add a test that registers a session over a local socket the way the
client library does, drops the client and checks that the error reaches
socketError(). Without this change it fails on Qt 6.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/sailfishos/sensorfw/pull/38]
---
 core/sockethandler.cpp                    | 12 ++++
 rpm/sensorfw-qt5.spec                     |  1 +
 tests/sockethandler/sockethandler.pro     | 21 ++++++
 tests/sockethandler/sockethandlertest.cpp | 86 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/tests.pro                           |  3 +-
 tests/tests.xml.in                        |  3 +
 6 files changed, 125 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/sockethandler/sockethandler.pro
 create mode 100644 tests/sockethandler/sockethandlertest.cpp

diff --git a/core/sockethandler.cpp b/core/sockethandler.cpp
index 96c841a..7bc65aa 100644
--- a/core/sockethandler.cpp
+++ b/core/sockethandler.cpp
@@ -259,8 +259,12 @@ bool SocketHandler::removeSession(int sessionId)
     if (socket) {
         disconnect(socket, SIGNAL(readyRead()), this, SLOT(socketReadable()));
         disconnect(socket, SIGNAL(disconnected()), this, SLOT(socketDisconnected()));
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0)
+        disconnect(socket, &QLocalSocket::errorOccurred, this, &SocketHandler::socketError);
+#else
         disconnect(socket, SIGNAL(error(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError)),
                    this, SLOT(socketError(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError)));
+#endif
         socket->deleteLater();
     }
 
@@ -287,8 +291,16 @@ void SocketHandler::newConnection()
         QLocalSocket* socket = m_server->nextPendingConnection();
         connect(socket, SIGNAL(readyRead()), this, SLOT(socketReadable()));
         connect(socket, SIGNAL(disconnected()), this, SLOT(socketDisconnected()));
+        // QLocalSocket::error(LocalSocketError) became errorOccurred() in
+        // Qt 5.15 and is gone in Qt 6, where connecting to it by name only
+        // printed a warning and socket errors went unhandled. Connect by
+        // pointer there, so a missing signal fails the build instead.
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(5, 15, 0)
+        connect(socket, &QLocalSocket::errorOccurred, this, &SocketHandler::socketError);
+#else
         connect(socket, SIGNAL(error(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError)),
                 this, SLOT(socketError(QLocalSocket::LocalSocketError)));
+#endif
 
         // Initialize socket
         socket->write("\n", 1);
